;;; Load-negative — a `rule` with no `:assert` and an `hrule` with no `:match`.
;;;
;;; Both halves of a declarator are required, and the message accumulates:
;;; two errors in the rule pass, in form order. `rule_missing_assert.ein` and
;;; `rule_missing_match.ein` pin each one alone; this pins them together, and
;;; it is also a **syntax probe** — the rule views draw a half-specified rule
;;; from the parsed forms, which no loadable file contains.
;;;
;;; One of the eighteen node-kind fixtures. As corpus entries they are
;;; rendered under every parse view and every op, and each rendering is
;;; digested by `corpus_shapes.md5`, so a change to how any of these
;;; shapes is drawn moves a digest. They exist because no *puzzle*
;;; contains these shapes.

(rule only-match () :match (r ?a ?b))
(hrule h () :assert (r a b))
